---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
export const prerender = true;
const baseUrl = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, "");
const lastUpdated = "May 15, 2026";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy — Tape"
  description="What Tape collects, why, who sees it, and what your rights are."
>
  <article class="legal-root">
    <p class="legal-eyebrow">Privacy</p>
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="legal-updated">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>

    <p class="lead">
      Tape is built by Keller Scholl and runs at
      tape.io. The short version: I collect the minimum
      needed to run the site, I don't sell any of it, I don't use it
      for advertising, and I don't share it with anyone except the
      service providers listed below.
    </p>

    <h2>What I collect</h2>

    <p>
      <strong>Email addresses</strong> if you submit one via the signup
      form. Stored in my Supabase database. Used only to send the
      newsletter (once launched) and to reply if you email me about
      Enterprise Support.
    </p>

    <p>
      <strong>Google account identifier, email, and name</strong> if
      you sign in with Google. I request the minimum OAuth scopes
      (<code>openid email</code>). Stored in my Supabase auth database.
      Used only to associate your saved dashboards with your account
      and to display your name on the <code>/me/</code> page.
    </p>

    <p>
      <strong>Saved dashboards</strong> if you create them. The
      composed state — section titles, chart references, your written
      notes — is stored in Supabase. By default, dashboards are public
      and visible to anyone who has the URL; you can mark a dashboard
      private, which restricts it to your signed-in account.
    </p>

    <p>
      <strong>Anonymous usage analytics</strong> via PostHog and Vercel
      Web Analytics. PostHog assigns an anonymous identifier stored in
      your browser's localStorage so I can see things like "how many
      people opened a chart" and "which composer features get used."
      No personally identifying information is sent to PostHog. The
      identifier resets if you clear your browser storage.
    </p>

    <p>
      <strong>IP addresses, temporarily</strong>, for rate limiting.
      When you submit the signup form or save a dashboard, I record
      the request's IP in a database table for up to 24 hours to
      prevent spam and bot abuse. Records older than that are deleted
      automatically.
    </p>

    <h2>What I don't collect</h2>

    <ul>
      <li>Payment information (there's nothing to pay for yet)</li>
      <li>Browsing history outside of tape.io</li>
      <li>Real-time location</li>
      <li>Cookies used for advertising or cross-site tracking</li>
      <li>Anything from your Google account beyond email and your name</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Who sees the data</h2>

    <p>
      I use three external services that necessarily process some of
      your data on my behalf:
    </p>

    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Supabase</strong> — database + auth. Stores email
        signups, Google OAuth identifiers, and saved dashboards.
        SOC 2 Type 2 certified.
        Their privacy policy:
        <a href="https://supabase.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">supabase.com/privacy</a>.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Vercel</strong> — hosting + page-view analytics. Sees
        request IP addresses (needed to deliver the page), basic HTTP
        metadata, and page-view counts.
        <a href="https://vercel.com/legal/privacy-policy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">vercel.com/legal/privacy-policy</a>.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>PostHog</strong> — custom event analytics. Receives the
        events I send (e.g. <code>chart_expanded</code>,
        <code>compose_share_copied</code>) along with the anonymous
        PostHog identifier.
        <a href="https://posthog.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">posthog.com/privacy</a>.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <p>
      I don't sell or rent data to anyone. I don't share data with
      advertisers, because I don't run ads. If law enforcement or a
      court requires data disclosure, I'll comply with valid legal
      process and, where lawful, notify you first.
    </p>

    <h2>Your rights</h2>

    <p>
      If you're in the EU (GDPR) or California (CCPA), you have explicit
      rights to access, correct, port, and delete your personal data.
      I'll honor any of those rights regardless of where you live — email
      me at <a href="mailto:keller.scholl@gmail.com">keller.scholl@gmail.com</a>
      and I'll handle it within seven days.
    </p>

    <p>
      For some of this you can self-serve:
    </p>

    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>See what's stored about you:</strong>
        <code>/me/</code> lists your saved dashboards.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Delete a dashboard:</strong> the
        <code>/me/</code> page has a delete button for each saved
        dashboard.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Delete your account entirely:</strong> email me with the
        request. I'll delete the Supabase auth row plus every saved
        dashboard you own.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Unsubscribe from email:</strong> every newsletter email
        will have an unsubscribe link, once the newsletter is set up.
        Before then, email me directly.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Data retention</h2>

    <ul>
      <li><strong>Email signups:</strong> kept until you ask me to delete it.</li>
      <li><strong>Account + saved dashboards:</strong> kept until you delete them or close the account.</li>
      <li><strong>PostHog analytics:</strong> 12 months (PostHog default).</li>
      <li><strong>Vercel page-view analytics:</strong> 12 months (Vercel default).</li>
      <li><strong>Rate-limit IP records:</strong> 24 hours, then automatically deleted.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Security</h2>

    <p>
      The site runs on Vercel's infrastructure with HTTPS everywhere.
      Authentication is via Google OAuth — I never see your password.
      Saved dashboards are protected by row-level security in
      Supabase: only the owner can read, edit, or delete their own
      rows (regardless of visibility setting; public dashboards can be
      read by anyone with the URL, but only the owner can modify them).
    </p>

    <p>
      No system is perfect. If there's a security incident affecting
      your personal data, I'll notify you by email within 72 hours of
      becoming aware of it.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>

    <p>
      Keller Scholl —
      <a href="mailto:keller.scholl@gmail.com">keller.scholl@gmail.com</a>.
      I read everything that comes in.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>

    <p>
      If I change this policy, I'll update the "Last updated" date at
      the top. For significant changes (new categories of data, new
      service providers, expanded data sharing), I'll email registered
      users in advance.
    </p>

    <p class="footer-note">
      <a href={baseUrl || "/"}>&larr; All dashboards</a>
      ·
      <a href={`${baseUrl}/terms/`}>Terms of Service</a>
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .legal-root {
    max-width: 680px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 64px 24px 96px;
    color: var(--color-neutral-900);
    line-height: 1.65;
  }
  .legal-eyebrow {
    font-size: 11px;
    font-weight: 600;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    color: var(--color-neutral-500);
    margin: 0 0 16px;
  }
  .legal-root h1 {
    font-size: var(--text-3xl);
    font-weight: 600;
    margin: 0 0 8px;
    line-height: 1.1;
    letter-spacing: -0.025em;
  }
  .legal-updated {
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    color: var(--color-neutral-500);
    margin: 0 0 32px;
  }
  .legal-root h2 {
    font-size: var(--text-base);
    font-weight: 600;
    margin: 40px 0 8px;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    color: var(--color-neutral-500);
  }
  .legal-root p,
  .legal-root ul {
    margin: 12px 0;
    color: var(--color-neutral-700);
    font-size: var(--text-base);
  }
  .legal-root ul {
    padding-left: 20px;
  }
  .legal-root li {
    margin: 6px 0;
  }
  .legal-root .lead {
    font-size: var(--text-lg);
    color: var(--color-neutral-800);
    margin-top: 0;
    line-height: 1.55;
  }
  .legal-root strong {
    color: var(--color-neutral-900);
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .legal-root code {
    font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace;
    background: var(--color-neutral-100);
    padding: 1px 4px;
    border-radius: 3px;
    font-size: 0.92em;
  }
  .legal-root a {
    color: var(--color-accent);
  }
  .footer-note {
    margin-top: 48px;
    padding-top: 16px;
    border-top: 1px solid rgba(55, 53, 47, 0.08);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
  }
</style>
